.Xr zfs-send 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
has created kldload's virtual machines since the first KVM profile.
On 2026-09-29, writing this page, its checks were tightened: a name had
been used as a dataset path unchecked, bad values were reported on
standard output with the exit status of a failed create, and a failed
clean-up or database registration was silent.
.Fl -vnc-listen
was added the same day.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Every machine's VNC console listens on every interface of the host with no
password, unless
.Fl -vnc-listen
says otherwise: anyone who can reach the host can see and type into the
console.
On a host on an untrusted network, use
.Fl -vnc-listen Ar 127.0.0.1 .
.Pp
The
.Pa rpool/vms@pre-create-
snapshots are not a way back: they hold the parent dataset only.
To be able to return a machine to an earlier state, snapshot it with
.Xr kvm-snap 8 .
.Pp
.Nm
assumes the pool is called
.Ql rpool
and machines live in
.Pa rpool/vms .
